WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.270 --> 00:00:01.970
Welcome back to Drew's News.

2
00:00:01.970 --> 00:00:03.440
We have a a legend at the desk.

3
00:00:03.440 --> 00:00:06.340
She's a writer with many best selling titles under her belt.

4
00:00:06.340 --> 00:00:08.470
A little book called Sex In The City

5
00:00:08.470 --> 00:00:10.250
launched one of the biggest cultural

6
00:00:10.250 --> 00:00:11.870
phenomenons of our time.

7
00:00:11.870 --> 00:00:13.523
Please welcome Candice Bushnell.

8
00:00:16.120 --> 00:00:19.380
I am so thrilled to be here

9
00:00:19.380 --> 00:00:21.850
because we saw each other at a fashion show.

10
00:00:21.850 --> 00:00:23.080
And I said Candice.

11
00:00:23.080 --> 00:00:24.100
You said come on the show,

12
00:00:24.100 --> 00:00:25.310
and I said, I'd love to,

13
00:00:25.310 --> 00:00:26.850
and you made it happen.

14
00:00:26.850 --> 00:00:29.128
Girl, you've got the power.

15
00:00:29.128 --> 00:00:30.593
Well,

16
00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:34.540
unlike Mark Cuban,

17
00:00:34.540 --> 00:00:36.580
who I shyly did not approach,

18
00:00:36.580 --> 00:00:38.970
we were luckily enough to get to converse

19
00:00:38.970 --> 00:00:43.053
and I mean, I'm such a fan,

20
00:00:43.912 --> 00:00:46.632
and an admirer of Sex In The City,

21
00:00:46.632 --> 00:00:51.610
and I'm curious where your book ends

22
00:00:51.610 --> 00:00:54.460
and the series continues to go on,

23
00:00:54.460 --> 00:00:58.330
what is your feelings and opinions of everything?

24
00:00:58.330 --> 00:01:02.093
I mean, you literally launched a cultural phenomenon!

25
00:01:02.936 --> 00:01:05.530
Well actually, it's been amazing,

26
00:01:05.530 --> 00:01:10.530 line:15%
and it's amazing that the show has lasted for so long

27
00:01:10.740 --> 00:01:13.680 line:15%
and so many iterations,

28
00:01:13.680 --> 00:01:15.970
but at the same time,

29
00:01:15.970 --> 00:01:19.637
Sex In The City is actually a small part of my career

30
00:01:19.637 --> 00:01:23.480
and I've written several best selling books

31
00:01:23.480 --> 00:01:25.780
and I've had two other TV shows,

32
00:01:25.780 --> 00:01:27.432
LipStick Jungle and The Carrie Diaries.

33
00:01:27.432 --> 00:01:29.928
I love both!

34
00:01:29.928 --> 00:01:30.761
Love,

35
00:01:32.440 --> 00:01:35.900
and my new book and my new stage show

36
00:01:35.900 --> 00:01:38.340
which I wrote and performed in called

37
00:01:38.340 --> 00:01:40.200
Is There Still Sex in the City

38
00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:43.100
is really about an exploration of

39
00:01:43.100 --> 00:01:48.100
the Sex In The City woman, in her 50's and 60's.

40
00:01:48.370 --> 00:01:53.370
So that's something that I'm going to continue with that

41
00:01:53.370 --> 00:01:56.744
and try to turn that into a TV series.

42
00:01:56.744 --> 00:02:01.500 line:15%
One thing that I do love is again relationships

43
00:02:01.500 --> 00:02:05.640 line:15%
and being the queen of New York dating and columns

44
00:02:05.640 --> 00:02:07.270 line:15%
and everything that you are and do,

45
00:02:07.270 --> 00:02:08.700
I was wondering if you want to head to

46
00:02:08.700 --> 00:02:10.210
the dating headlines with us.

47
00:02:10.210 --> 00:02:12.060
I absolutely would.

48
00:02:12.060 --> 00:02:13.740
Okay, let's take it away.

49
00:02:13.740 --> 00:02:14.573
First headline.

50
00:02:15.574 --> 00:02:16.407
Wear my glasses.

51
00:02:18.272 --> 00:02:21.490
Okay, there's so many new dating terms,

52
00:02:21.490 --> 00:02:22.950
it's hard to keep track.

53
00:02:22.950 --> 00:02:24.870
Now Elite Daily reports

54
00:02:24.870 --> 00:02:25.990
that there's a word for when

55
00:02:25.990 --> 00:02:29.140
you get all dressed up, hair done, makeup ready,

56
00:02:29.140 --> 00:02:33.650
dressed to the nines only to have your date text and cancel.

57
00:02:33.650 --> 00:02:35.640 line:15%
It's called glam-boozled

58
00:02:37.190 --> 00:02:40.790 line:15%
and a dating survey says that 58% of daters

59
00:02:40.790 --> 00:02:43.020 line:15%
say they've been glam-boozled.

60
00:02:43.020 --> 00:02:45.840 line:15%
A good rule of thumb is if you haven't heard from him

61
00:02:45.840 --> 00:02:50.840 line:15%
an hour before the date, hold off on those lashes.

62
00:02:51.010 --> 00:02:52.000
Now the question is,

63
00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:54.890
have either one of you been glam-boozled,

64
00:02:54.890 --> 00:02:57.540
or have you been the glam-boozler?

65
00:02:57.540 --> 00:02:58.373
Try it.

66
00:02:58.373 --> 00:02:59.520
You try to glam-boozle me,

67
00:02:59.520 --> 00:03:01.220
you better show up with a receipt,

68
00:03:01.220 --> 00:03:02.900
a doctor's note or a neck brace.

69
00:03:02.900 --> 00:03:04.244
I'm sorry.

70
00:03:04.244 --> 00:03:06.120
Not happening.

71
00:03:06.120 --> 00:03:07.630
You don't get a date number two.

72
00:03:07.630 --> 00:03:11.363
How many people in the audience have been glam-boozled?

73
00:03:13.600 --> 00:03:14.910
Not that many of us.

74
00:03:14.910 --> 00:03:16.400
Either we're not being honest

75
00:03:16.400 --> 00:03:19.093
or there's a very lucky audience here.

76
00:03:20.130 --> 00:03:21.983
Okay, who has glam-boozled?

77
00:03:23.190 --> 00:03:24.210
No one's gonna admit.

78
00:03:24.210 --> 00:03:25.370
Did somebody admit that?

79
00:03:25.370 --> 00:03:27.340
Yes, you did!

80
00:03:27.340 --> 00:03:28.380
I love it.

81
00:03:28.380 --> 00:03:30.820
You have a microphone and a camera coming to you.

82
00:03:30.820 --> 00:03:33.093
Aren't you so glad you raised your hand, sir?

83
00:03:36.080 --> 00:03:38.780
Why did you glam-boozle someone?

84
00:03:38.780 --> 00:03:40.920
I got nervous and scared.

85
00:03:40.920 --> 00:03:42.300
We've all done it.

86
00:03:42.300 --> 00:03:43.253
You're all liars.

87
00:03:45.926 --> 00:03:47.320
How interesting that is,

88
00:03:47.320 --> 00:03:49.380
because you got nervous and scared.

89
00:03:49.380 --> 00:03:52.054
See, it wasn't even about the other person.

90
00:03:52.054 --> 00:03:53.300
And that's why someone's gonna take that

91
00:03:53.300 --> 00:03:54.890
and be like, what's wrong with me?

92
00:03:54.890 --> 00:03:56.220
That's what I did.

93
00:03:56.220 --> 00:03:57.520
Someone stood me up

94
00:03:57.520 --> 00:04:00.070
and I thought God, did they hear something about me

95
00:04:00.070 --> 00:04:02.600
and I went through this whole laundry list

96
00:04:02.600 --> 00:04:04.630
and I just thought, you know what?

97
00:04:04.630 --> 00:04:06.420
No, they don't know me.

98
00:04:06.420 --> 00:04:08.010
They don't know anything about me,

99
00:04:08.010 --> 00:04:09.630
and this is on them,

100
00:04:09.630 --> 00:04:11.730
and I just need to carry on with my afternoon

101
00:04:11.730 --> 00:04:14.400
and not make this a reason to self loathe.

102
00:04:14.400 --> 00:04:15.233
Forget it.

103
00:04:15.233 --> 00:04:16.680
Buh bye.

104
00:04:16.680 --> 00:04:18.502
What about this, you guys.

105
00:04:18.502 --> 00:04:19.950
Vogue is asking this important question.

106
00:04:19.950 --> 00:04:21.670
What do you call the person

107
00:04:21.670 --> 00:04:24.740
that you've just started dating?

108
00:04:24.740 --> 00:04:26.690
When Carrie dated the Russian on Sex In The City,

109
00:04:26.690 --> 00:04:28.850
remember she said, I've taken a lover.

110
00:04:28.850 --> 00:04:29.793 line:15%
You remember that?

111
00:04:30.647 --> 00:04:31.522 line:15%
Lover.

112
00:04:31.522 --> 00:04:32.820 line:15%
Yes,

113
00:04:32.820 --> 00:04:35.500 line:15%
but that quote doesn't work for everybody,

114
00:04:35.500 --> 00:04:37.590 line:15%
because if you just say it's the person I'm dating,

115
00:04:37.590 --> 00:04:39.060 line:15%
that can feel clunky, right?

116
00:04:39.060 --> 00:04:41.570 line:15%
So Vogue suggests some other options.

117
00:04:41.570 --> 00:04:44.840 line:15%
They call them your flame, your extended fling,

118
00:04:44.840 --> 00:04:46.740 line:15%
your suitor, your crush.

119
00:04:46.740 --> 00:04:48.480 line:15%
God, I don't like any of these.

120
00:04:48.480 --> 00:04:49.958 line:15%
I feel like.

121
00:04:49.958 --> 00:04:50.960 line:15%
I say my future ex husband.

122
00:04:50.960 --> 00:04:53.030 line:15%
That's good!

123
00:04:53.030 --> 00:04:55.250 line:15%
Problem solved, right.

124
00:04:55.250 --> 00:04:57.470
I think though if you're starting to call

125
00:04:57.470 --> 00:04:59.350
who you're just seeing, something,

126
00:04:59.350 --> 00:05:01.200
they're gonna stop calling you back,

127
00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:03.430
because that just seems like too much pressure.

128
00:05:03.430 --> 00:05:04.800
No?

129
00:05:04.800 --> 00:05:05.990
Yes.

130
00:05:05.990 --> 00:05:08.403
Well for me, the word lover,

131
00:05:08.403 --> 00:05:11.280
that is a strange thing,

132
00:05:11.280 --> 00:05:13.380
for me to call somebody,

133
00:05:13.380 --> 00:05:16.020
because it feels like it's French.

134
00:05:16.020 --> 00:05:17.730
Nothing against French people

135
00:05:18.720 --> 00:05:21.180
and also something that when you're married

136
00:05:21.180 --> 00:05:22.410
you have lovers.

137
00:05:22.410 --> 00:05:26.435
I always think of French married people having lovers.

138
00:05:26.435 --> 00:05:28.067
Oh, like a mistress.

139
00:05:28.067 --> 00:05:28.900
Like you're a cuckold.

140
00:05:30.140 --> 00:05:30.973
An adulterer.

141
00:05:30.973 --> 00:05:33.010
Yes, exactly.

142
00:05:33.010 --> 00:05:34.770
Well, I would say,

143
00:05:34.770 --> 00:05:36.343
I would just call it yay.

144
00:05:37.394 --> 00:05:38.979
That would be my term.

145
00:05:38.979 --> 00:05:39.970
Well thank you Candice Bushnell.

146
00:05:39.970 --> 00:05:44.321
I am so glad that you had come by the desk

147
00:05:44.321 --> 00:05:47.091
and come and do this with us.

148
00:05:47.091 --> 00:05:49.360
Now Candice is taking her one woman show

149
00:05:49.360 --> 00:05:51.310
Is There Still Sex In The City

150
00:05:51.310 --> 00:05:53.410
out on the road later this year,

151
00:05:53.410 --> 00:05:55.750 line:15%
so make sure to look out for that

152
00:05:55.750 --> 00:05:58.350 line:15%
and don't get glam-boozled or don't glam-boozle

153
00:05:58.350 --> 00:06:00.150 line:15%
and let's all be good to each other

154
00:06:00.150 --> 00:06:01.843 line:15%
and we'll be right back.

155
00:06:01.843 --> 00:06:04.510 line:15%
(upbeat music)

